<title>PHILIPPINES: Liberty Telecom up 5.8 pct to 1.10 pesos.</title>
<headline>Liberty Telecom up 5.8 pct to 1.10 pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Liberty Telecommunications rose six centavos, or 5.8 percent, to 1.10 pesos in midsession on Tuesday on news its board decided to enter into an agreement with South Korea's LG Group, traders said.  </p>
<p>&quot;That's the one (the news) that's perking it up,&quot; said Harry Liu, president of Summit Securities.</p>
<p>Liberty Telecom said on Monday its joint venture with LG Information and Communications Ltd will introduce personal communication services. This operates like a cellular phone but operates on a higher band so it can reach a bigger subsrcriber base.</p>
<p>Volume of shares traded reached 3.07 million valued at 3.45 million pesos.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom (632) 841-8937</p>
</text>
